{
  "v": 11,
  "label": "a listing carrying another body at the revision the base holds, over a local edit, is the both-changed case: manual conflicts and pushes nothing",
  "note": "the local body c2 left the base c1 at r1. The server edited the card without moving its ETag: the listing names r1 again and carries c3. Read as a revision the base does not hold, it is the both-changed case: manual marks the binding conflicted at r1, the base's own revision, with c3 as conflict_object, the item keeping c2 and its summary, and nothing is pushed. Reading the revision alone would push c2 gated on r1, which the server accepts, over c3 unread (SYNC.md section 5, A carried body is a remote edit under an unmoved revision; vector 13 the same case at a moved revision)",
